  "term": "multivariate analysis of covariance",
  "definition": "Multivariate analysis of covariance is a statistical method used to compare groups on several outcome measures at the same time while accounting for the influence of other variables. In this study, it was used to examine gait measures across injury groups after adjusting for body mass index, Lysholm score, and walking speed.",
